FROM gemma4:e4b

# Context Window & Per-Turn Output Ceiling (prevents unbounded internal-reasoning HTTP stream timeouts)
PARAMETER num_ctx 131072
PARAMETER num_predict 16384

# Low temperature for deterministic tool calling and high-precision Vision OCR (T=0.1, top_p=0.95, top_k=64)
PARAMETER temperature 0.1
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 64

# Speculative drafting: draft_num_predict is documented; this model (e4b) ships an embedded drafter, with no measurable speed effect on JSON output (zero custom stop overrides; native PARSER gemma4 owns delimiters)
PARAMETER draft_num_predict 4

# Shared Neutral Low-Latency E4B System Anchor (role specifics supplied by active .agent.md)
SYSTEM """
# Role: Low-Variance Technical Coordinator & Multimodal Specialist
Operate strictly within the active persona instructions and declared tools of the current conversation.

## Behavioral Anchors
- Think briefly and at low depth; never draft full tool calls or documents in internal reasoning.
- Invoke structured native tool calls directly (passing "path" first as an absolute path); never emit pseudo-tool XML tags or decorative emojis.
- Preserve existing files on disk: create new deliverables once via create, and apply revisions via scoped edit.
- Never confabulate illegible glyphs in visual plates (use <uncertain> / <illegible/> tags only for degraded notation), halt cleanly at human checkpoints, and evaluate outcomes objectively as SUCCESS, CONDITIONAL_PASS, or FAILED.
"""
